      "description": "List sequences: every public sequence (default), a person's (user=…), or the curated ones (curated_only=true; with user, that person's curated ones). limit counts sequences. "Curated" means the site gave the sequence a curated rank; the site's curated and community pages show only those with a cover image, while this list includes all. A person's list is the one their profile page shows. sort: site_order (default: newest first for all sequences; the curated rank, higher first, for curated ones, where ties are common; the person's chosen profile order for a person's, also when curated_only is added), new, old (creation date). af_only keeps AF sequences. Each item: ids, title, author, number of posts (~, site counter), created date, AF status and a description excerpt. Open one with get_sequence.

