    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": true,
        "readOnlyHint": true,
      },
      "description": "Edit history of a post or a wiki page's text, or the wiki edits of a person: exactly one of post, tag (a lens slug or summary_id gives that lens's or summary's own history) or user (wiki edits only; post histories are read one post at a time). A comment's earlier versions are not available. Without revision: the publicly visible versions, newest first (sort old for oldest first; limit counts versions), each with revision_id, version, date, editor, the forum's own count of characters added and removed (it can differ from the change between the versions listed) and labels such as "2019 import snapshot", "image copy to CDN", "before publication"; plus which version is the original, the one current when the post was published (if the posting date was reset later, that version may already include early edits). With user: their wiki edits, newest first, each with its page (for people with more than 2,000 wiki revisions, only the first 2,000 the forum returns can be ordered, and the last page says so). revision=<revision_id>|original|current returns that version's text (match=<text> keeps only the paragraphs containing it; match reads whole words, ignoring case and accents and reading punctuation as a space; phrases does not); adding compare_to=<revision_id>|original|previous|current returns the word-level changes between the two versions instead (computed here). phrases=[…] checks each phrase separately in the original and the current text and, if it was added later, finds the first version containing it (assuming it was not removed and re-added); long histories may need the cursor to finish. Limits: post texts from before 13 February 2019 exist only as a migration snapshot dated to the original posting time, so their original wording and earlier edits are not available; some later posts' visible history starts after publication ("published text not available"); version numbers have gaps and can repeat (always use revision ids); "all public versions listed" is never a complete edit timeline; titles have no history. A post's text comes from that version's page, as a logged-out reader sees it; a version whose page can't be read gives an error, and a version saved between February and July 2026 shows [equation] where its page holds no equation text.

